= Introduction
Over recent years, digital learning platforms have become important tools for supporting teaching, learning, and assessment in higher education. They provide access to learning materials, structure learning activities, and can support student engagement and learning processes @bondMappingResearchStudent2020.

The research group for Applied Education Technologies at the Technical University of Munich develops Artemis, an interactive learning platform. It supports automated and manual assessment workflows for different exercise types and provides immediate feedback in programming education. The platform supports managing courses, exercises, exams, submissions, and grading processes @kruscheArTEMiSAutomaticAssessment2018. 
